& [CanonicalRecord: IR2ImplementationActivation] is the processed planning authority for IR2 bounded implementation activation slices
  + [canonical_uuid] is 418bcf74-48cf-4d72-90f3-670d0698b0d1
  + [source_manifest_uuid] is dcf9737f-dccc-4b6d-b7f2-762a73011483
  + [slice_surface_uuid] is 7a6698a5-7638-4811-8608-8e843e82bc5a
  + [authority_scope] is IR2 implementation activation slice order, gates, file inventory, fixture creation boundary, test/proof boundary, model routing, generated artifact limits, and downstream gate preservation
  + [implementation_scope] is bounded parser/projection implementation and proof work only
  + [depends_on] is docs/reviews/IR2_Completion_Review.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/planning/IR2_Authority_Projection_Pack.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/implementation/IR2_Parser_Projection_Implementation_Plan.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/fixtures/IR2_Parser_Projection_Fixture_Plan.v1.sop

  = must: use docs/slices/IR2_Implementation_Activation_Slices.v1.sop as the current IR2 implementation activation slice surface
  = must: execute IR2-IA01 before creating implementation or fixture files
  = must: run completion review after each activation or implementation slice before opening the next gated slice
  = must: preserve accepted IR2 authority semantics; implementation slices may encode accepted behavior but may not change parser, extraction, validation, projection, fixture, or generated artifact policy
  = must: keep all generated artifacts non-authoritative and rebuildable
  - never: treat these activation slices as permission for LangGraph runtime work, surface work, adapter work, operations simulator work, operations control, or live machine control

& [CanonicalIR2ImplementationActivationSliceSet] is the bounded implementation activation slice sequence
  + [slice] is IR2-IA01 bounded implementation activation boundary and file inventory confirmation
  + [slice] is IR2-IA02 fixture source and expected-ledger seed material
  + [slice] is IR2-IA03 authority discovery and SOP parser implementation
  + [slice] is IR2-IA04 KernelRecord extraction and validation implementation
  + [slice] is IR2-IA05 SQLite projection schema, writer, and rebuild implementation
  + [slice] is IR2-IA06 parser/projection contract test integration and generated-output proof
  + [slice] is IR2-IA07 implementation completion review and parser/projection proof pack

  = must: preserve this order unless a completion review rebakes IR2 implementation activation
  = must: mark downstream slices stale when an upstream accepted output changes

& [CanonicalIR2ImplementationActivationGate] is the activation rule for bounded implementation work
  + [current_ready_slice] is IR2-IA01
  + [gated_slice] is IR2-IA02 until IR2-IA01 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR2-IA03 until IR2-IA02 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR2-IA04 until IR2-IA03 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR2-IA05 until IR2-IA04 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR2-IA06 until IR2-IA05 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR2-IA07 until IR2-IA06 accepted
  + [completion_gate] is parser/projection implementation proof pack accepted after IR2-IA07

  = must: expose only IR2-IA01 as ready right now
  = must: keep code and fixture file creation gated until IR2-IA01 confirms the activation boundary

& [CanonicalIR2ImplementationActivationModelRouting] is the model-routing record
  + [IR2-IA01] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [IR2-IA02] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable after IR2-IA01 acceptance because fixture and expected-ledger seed material is bounded by accepted contracts
  + [IR2-IA03] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable after IR2-IA02 acceptance because discovery and parser implementation is bounded by accepted parser profile and fixture expectations
  + [IR2-IA04] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable after IR2-IA03 acceptance because extraction and validation implementation is bounded by accepted mappings and expected ledgers
  + [IR2-IA05] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable after IR2-IA04 acceptance because SQLite projection implementation is bounded by accepted schema and generated artifact policy
  + [IR2-IA06] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable after IR2-IA05 acceptance because contract tests and generated-output proof are bounded by accepted fixture and implementation outputs
  + [IR2-IA07] is requires deeper reasoning

  = must: state Spark suitability explicitly for bounded implementation, fixture, test, and proof-update work
  = must: preserve deeper reasoning for activation boundary confirmation, final proof acceptance, and any semantic or downstream-gate change

& [CanonicalIR2ImplementationActivationForbiddenScope] is the forbidden scope record
  + [forbidden_scope] is external dependency addition
  + [forbidden_scope] is implementation file outside accepted inventory
  + [forbidden_scope] is source authority mutation
  + [forbidden_scope] is generated projection authority promotion
  + [forbidden_scope] is LangGraph runtime implementation
  + [forbidden_scope] is UI or surface implementation
  + [forbidden_scope] is adapter implementation
  + [forbidden_scope] is operations simulator implementation
  + [forbidden_scope] is operations control
  + [forbidden_scope] is live machine control

  = must: fail any slice review that detects forbidden scope

